{#
  REAPER's Linux dialog theming: the theme's own libSwell-user.colortheme,
  rendered line-for-line with this repo's metric overrides substituted in.

  Why a template instead of a plain copy of the file: the vendored asset stays
  BYTE-IDENTICAL to what the Reapertips package ships, so the next theme update
  can still be diffed against it (that diff is how the v1.93b update was shown
  to touch only two files). The size overrides live in the task's vars, where
  they are visible and tunable, instead of being edited into a vendored blob
  where the next update would silently revert them.

  Only keys listed in reaper_swell_metrics are rewritten; every other line —
  colours, comments, blanks — passes through untouched. A key we override that
  upstream later renames would silently stop applying, so if a dialog ever
  reverts to looking cramped after a theme update, diff the vendored file's
  first lines against these keys.

  LAYOUT IS LOAD-BEARING: each emitted line's newline must follow an
  EXPRESSION tag (}}), never a block tag. Ansible templates run with
  trim_blocks=True, which eats the newline immediately after {% endif %} /
  {% endfor %} — writing this loop the obvious way collapses all 93 lines into
  one, and SWELL then parses only the first key (caught by rendering it). Same
  family as the reaper-mouse.ini escape trap: whitespace here is data.
-#}
{% for line in reaper_swell_vendor_lines %}{% set key = line.split(' ') | first %}{% if key in reaper_swell_metrics %}{{ key }} {{ reaper_swell_metrics[key] }}
{% else %}{{ line }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
